---
<section class="home-hero">
  <img class="home-hero-bg" src="/images/grouper-tampa-bay.webp" alt="Guest holding a gag grouper on Tampa Bay" fetchpriority="high" width="1400" height="1133">
  <div class="wrap home-hero-inner">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Private charters · Tampa Bay, Gulf &amp; Central Florida lakes</p>
    <h1>Tampa Bay Fishing Charters for <span class="hl">Whatever You Came to Catch</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-lead">Maybe it's your kid's first redfish on a calm morning in the mangroves. Maybe it's a cooler of snapper and grouper off Gulf bottom, or a tarpon jumping beside the boat in July.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" href="{{ site.booking }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Reserve a Date</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href="/charters/">See Our Charters</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <svg class="wave wave-white" viewBox="0 0 1440 48" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 24C180 48 360 48 540 30S900 0 1080 12s270 30 360 24V48H0z"/></svg>
</section>

<section class="intro-strip">
  <div class="wrap intro-grid">
    <div class="intro-copy">
      <p>Our team of captains fishes inshore, nearshore, offshore and the lakes near Orlando. So whatever you have in mind and whenever you can get away, one of our captains is already out there doing it.</p>
      <p class="intro-stat">Between them, that's [95+] years of fishing and [850+] five star reviews.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="trust">
      <li><strong>10% deposit</strong><span>holds your date</span></li>
      <li><strong>Weather refund</strong><span>new date or your deposit back</span></li>
      <li><strong>Licenses included</strong><span>plus rods, reels, tackle &amp; bait</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Our charters</p>
    <h2>Pick the kind of day you want</h2>
    <div class="cards">
    {% for t in trips %}
      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-media"><img src="/images/{{ t.img }}.webp" alt="{{ t.alt }}" loading="lazy" width="1400" height="1050"><span class="price-tag">From {{ t.from }}</span></div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <h3>{{ t.name }} fishing charters</h3>
          <p>{{ t.line }}</p>
          <a class="more stretched" href="{{ t.url }}">{{ t.name }} trip details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </article>
    {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="chips"><p>After one fish in particular?</p>
      <a class="chip" href="/redfish/">Redfish</a><a class="chip" href="/snook/">Snook</a><a class="chip" href="/tarpon/">Tarpon</a><a class="chip" href="/grouper/">Grouper</a><a class="chip" href="/shark/">Shark</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-navy section has-wave">
  <svg class="wave wave-navy" viewBox="0 0 1440 48" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 24C180 48 360 48 540 30S900 0 1080 12s270 30 360 24V48H0z"/></svg>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head-row">
      <div><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Prices</p><h2>Tampa Bay fishing charter prices</h2>
      <p class="sub-lead" style="margin:0">Prices are per boat, not per person. Your captain, rods, reels, tackle, bait and <strong>fishing licenses</strong> are included.</p></div>
      <a class="btn btn-accent" href="{{ site.booking }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Reserve a Date</a>
    </div>
    <div class="rate-wrap"><table class="rate">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Trip</th><th scope="col">4 hours</th><th scope="col">6 hours</th><th scope="col">8 hours</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{% for r in prices %}<tr><th scope="row">{{ r.trip }}</th><td>{{ r.h4 }}</td><td>{{ r.h6 }}</td><td>{{ r.h8 }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody>
    </table></div>
    <p style="margin:16px 0 0">Book more than one tarpon trip and save $50 on each. Gift cards in any amount work for any trip. <a href="{{ site.giftCards }}" style="color:#fff;font-weight:700">Buy a gift card</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head-row"><div><p class="eyebrow">Your guides</p><h2>Meet our captains</h2></div><a class="link-arrow" href="/about/">All captain bios <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    <div class="captains">
      <div class="captain"><img src="/images/capt-ashmore.webp" alt="Capt. William Ashmore holding a redfish" loading="lazy" width="640" height="411">
        <h3>Capt. William "Dex" Ashmore</h3><p>Grew up in Florida and has fished Tampa Bay and Central Florida for more than 40 years. You may hear guests call him Dex.</p></div>
      <div class="captain"><img src="/images/capt-pruner.webp" alt="Capt. David Pruner on the boat" loading="lazy" width="1240" height="1023">
        <h3>Capt. David Pruner</h3><p>Learned to fish on Indiana lakes with his dad, who taught him that patience and persistence are what catch fish. He has been at it for 25 years.</p></div>
      <div class="captain"><img src="/images/capt-gonzales.webp" alt="Capt. Frankie Gonzales holding a snook" loading="lazy" width="619" height="826" style="object-position:top">
        <h3>Capt. Frankie Gonzales</h3><p>Has spent 30 years on the inshore water from Tampa Bay up into the southern Nature Coast.</p></div>
      <div class="captain"><img src="/images/capt-hahn.webp" alt="Capt. Rob Hahn holding a gag grouper" loading="lazy" width="1102" height="1400">
        <h3>Capt. Rob Hahn</h3><p>A Master Diver who has been underwater on the reefs and wrecks his guests fish, and knows where the fish there live and how they move.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-sand">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Reviews</p>
    <h2 class="display-md">What our guests say</h2>
    <div class="quotes">
    {% for r in reviews %}<blockquote class="quote"><p>"{{ r.quote }}"</p><footer>{{ r.name }}{% if r.note %}, {{ r.note }}{% endif %}</footer></blockquote>{% endfor %}
    </div>
    <p style="margin:28px 0 0"><a class="link-arrow" href="/reviews/">Read more reviews <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Seasons</p>
      <h2>Tampa Bay fishing through the year</h2>
      <div class="seasons">
      <div class="season"><h3>Spring</h3><p>Kingfish move north past the mouth of the bay, with the run peaking in April and May. Snook open for harvest again in March and April.</p></div>
      <div class="season"><h3>Summer</h3><p>Tarpon roll through the bay from May through August. By late summer, redfish start pushing in from the surrounding waters and the sharks stay busy.</p></div>
      <div class="season"><h3>Fall</h3><p>Schools of mullet push along the shorelines on their way to the Gulf, and snook, redfish, tarpon and sharks follow them. Kings come back through in October and November.</p></div>
      <div class="season"><h3>Winter</h3><p>Sheepshead stack up on reefs, rock piles, docks and bridge pilings, and the bottom fishing stays steady nearshore. It's also when the crappie bite on the lakes.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <img src="/images/family-shark-bow.webp" alt="A family on the bow watching a shark come up to the boat" loading="lazy" width="1400" height="1040" class="first-img">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:32px">New to fishing?</p>
      <h2>Your first fishing charter</h2>
      <p>You don't need to know anything before you step on the boat. Your captain rigs the rods, picks the spot and talks you through the bite, the hookset and the fight. Kids are welcome, and inshore and crappie trips are the easiest place for young anglers to start.</p>
      <p>We bring bottled water and ice. You bring food, other drinks, sunglasses, sunblock and clothes for the weather.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-navy section has-wave" id="areas">
  <svg class="wave wave-navy" viewBox="0 0 1440 48" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 24C180 48 360 48 540 30S900 0 1080 12s270 30 360 24V48H0z"/></svg>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Areas we fish</p>
    <h2 class="display-md">Where we fish</h2>
    <p class="sub-lead" style="font-size:19px;max-width:700px">Our boats launch from marinas around metro Tampa and fish the whole bay, from Apollo Beach on the east shore to St. Petersburg and Anna Maria near the mouth, out into the Gulf and inland to the lakes south of Orlando.</p>
    <div class="areas">
      <a class="area" href="/tampa-bay-fishing/"><strong>Tampa Bay</strong><span>The whole bay, flats to channels</span><span class="area-go" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a class="area" href="/apollo-beach-fishing/"><strong>Apollo Beach</strong><span>The east side of the bay</span><span class="area-go" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a class="area" href="/st-petersburg-fishing/"><strong>St. Petersburg</strong><span>Lower bay and the beaches</span><span class="area-go" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a class="area" href="/anna-maria-fishing/"><strong>Anna Maria</strong><span>The mouth of the bay</span><span class="area-go" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head-row"><div><p class="eyebrow">Fishing reports</p><h2>Latest from the water</h2></div><a class="link-arrow" href="/fishing-reports/">All fishing reports <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    <div class="reports">
    {% for r in collections.reports | head(3) %}
      <a class="report" href="{{ r.url }}"><img src="/images/{{ r.data.heroImg }}.webp" alt="{{ r.data.heroAlt }}" loading="lazy" width="1400" height="1000">
      <span class="meta">{{ r.date | monthYear }} · {{ r.data.author }}</span><span class="rt">{{ r.data.h1 or r.data.title }}</span></a>
    {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
